+# Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out; Filtering the Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Its provenance stayed open, like every row the survey produced.
+
+On 2026-10-25 the owner requested a filter that narrows the veterinarian directory to one specialty. Read literally, NG-9 forbids it. The owner decided the row at intake rather than leaving the conflict to interpretation.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Rejected by the owner: filtering by an attribute the directory already shows is wanted.
+2. **Remove NG-9 for veterinarians.** Rejected by the owner: free-text veterinarian search stays out.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined. Filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's words at intake: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+Free-text search for a veterinarian is now a decided non-goal, not a survey artifact. Narrowing the directory by an attribute it lists is permitted. Pet search and visit search are untouched by this decision and keep their open provenance.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The specialty filter on the veterinarian directory proceeds as a requirement of its own.
+- A request for name search, partial matching, or any other free-text lookup of a veterinarian meets a decided row. It proceeds only on a fresh owner decision recorded at intake.
+- This narrowing does not cover a filter on an attribute the directory does not show. Such a filter needs its own owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the filter the narrowing admits.
